f 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426355 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426355 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186426337 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426355 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "fae70d19-83f0-5b05-8643-3c518b988070" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426356 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426352 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426356 #edb/ref 1069 "q-91869" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426356 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426356 #edb/ref 1071 "Peter prepares $\\frac{1}{3}$ of a liter of coffee to distribute, in equal quantities, to his $5$ guests. How much coffee will each guest receive?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426356 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "0862a0c0-458a-56cf-9e21-ed5b94c7b818" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426356 #edb/ref 1074 "To find out how much coffee each guest will receive, we have to divide the amount of coffee by the number of guests:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷5\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷5=\\frac{1}{3\\times 5}=\\frac{1}{15}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each guest will receive $\\frac{1}{15}$ liters of coffee." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426357 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426353 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426357 #edb/ref 1069 "q-196435" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426357 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426357 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{1}{8}÷10=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426357 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "18bead9f-06cc-5538-86ff-ffa5437e0458" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426357 #edb/ref 1074 "To divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{8}÷10=\\frac{1}{8\\times 10}=\\frac{1}{80}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426358 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426341 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426358 #edb/ref 1069 "q-58372" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426358 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426358 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{1}{3}÷4=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426358 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "2ea75a7a-07dc-5c3b-a013-688d65828268" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426358 #edb/ref 1074 "To divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{3}÷4=\\frac{1}{3\\times 4}=\\frac{1}{12}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426359 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426342 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426359 #edb/ref 1069 "q-196454" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426359 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426359 #edb/ref 1071 "A farmer divided his field into $3$ smaller lots of equal area. What is the area of each lot if the total area of the field is $\\frac{1}{2}$ acres?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, the area of each lot is\n{{field-1}} acres." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426359 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "38810655-0448-5128-9773-0f9ac772e869" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426359 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine the area of each lot, we divide the total field area by the number of lots.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷3\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷3=\\frac{1}{2\\times 3}=\\frac{1}{6}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the area of each lot is $\\frac{1}{6}$ acres." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426360 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426344 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426360 #edb/ref 1069 "q-196446" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426360 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426360 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{1}{32}÷3=${{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426360 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3d3a7fc2-56f5-5b04-bad8-a5bc10e2751b" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426360 #edb/ref 1074 "To divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{32}÷3=\\frac{1}{32\\times 3}=\\frac{1}{96}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426361 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426348 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426361 #edb/ref 1069 "q-196453" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426361 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426361 #edb/ref 1071 "Zoe distributed $\\frac{1}{2}$ kilograms of sausage equally between $4$ cats. How much sausage did each cat receive?\n\nExpressed as a fraction, each cat received\n{{field-1}}  kilograms of sausage." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426361 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "3ecabb9b-a95d-572c-bb9e-7f166638bf38" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426361 #edb/ref 1074 "To determine the amount of sausage per cat, we must divide the amount of sausage by the number of cats.\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷4\n$$\n\nTo divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷4=\\frac{1}{2\\times 4}=\\frac{1}{8}\n$$\n\nTherefore, each cat received $\\frac{1}{8}$  kilograms of sausage." #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426362 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426345 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426362 #edb/ref 1069 "q-58398" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426362 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426362 #edb/ref 1071 "$\\frac{1}{2}÷30=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426362 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "526c1f45-2325-5364-aa6d-f9597d1795df" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426362 #edb/ref 1074 "To divide a unit fraction by a whole number, we multiply the fraction's denominator by that whole number:\n\n$$\n\\frac{1}{2}÷30=\\frac{1}{2\\times 30}=\\frac{1}{60}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426363 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186426349 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426363 #edb/ref 1069 "q-196442" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186426363 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 1759218604